Falsifies `address_space_layout::verification::pair_page_accepts_every_page_of_its_band`.

The defect: `pair_page` asks `window` for two pages, so the last page of `PAIR_PAGES` is refused.

Expected to fail: Kani reports "a window must lie wholly inside its band" reachable at `virtual_address = 0x0FFF_F000`.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@
 /// in the source; what the call adds is that an address outside [`PAIR_PAGES`], or not page
 /// aligned, stops the build instead of colliding with a runtime page at run time.
 pub const fn pair_page(virtual_address: u64) -> u64 {
-    window(PAIR_PAGES, virtual_address, PAGE_BYTES)
+    window(PAIR_PAGES, virtual_address, 2 * PAGE_BYTES)
 }
 
 /// **A runtime window's address, checked against the map at compile time.** As [`pair_page`], for
